# USSLP Store Gateway Unit configuration.
#
# Install to /etc/usslp/sgu.env, owner root:usslp, mode 0640.
#
# Every variable here is read through config.Loader with the USSLP_ prefix
# (platform/pkg/config/config.go). Every one of them is ALSO resolvable from a
# file: setting USSLP_MQTT_PASSWORD_FILE=/run/secrets/mqtt-password makes the
# loader read the file and ignore USSLP_MQTT_PASSWORD entirely. Use the _FILE
# form for anything secret — an environment file is world-readable to anything
# that can read /proc, and a mounted secret is not.
#
# The names below are the ones the binary actually reads. Anything not in this
# list is not a setting; edge/cmd/sgu/main.go is the authority.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Identity — required. The binary refuses to start without these two.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
USSLP_STORE_ID=REPLACE-ME
USSLP_TENANT_ID=REPLACE-ME

# The gateway's own identity. Defaults to "sgu-local", which is fine for one
# box and wrong for a fleet: it is what a support engineer greps for.
USSLP_SGU_ID=REPLACE-ME

# The region. It becomes the third segment of every MQTT topic
# (usslp/{tenant}/{region}/{store}/...) and a const label on every metric, so
# it must match the cloud region this store's traffic lands in.
USSLP_REGION=us-east-1

USSLP_ENVIRONMENT=prod
USSLP_LOG_LEVEL=info
USSLP_LOG_FORMAT=json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Listeners
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The store's MQTT broker. 0.0.0.0 deliberately: the controllers reach it over
# the store LAN, and the systemd unit's IPAddressAllow is what restricts who
# can. Do not narrow this to 127.0.0.1 unless the controllers are on this box.
USSLP_BROKER_ADDR=0.0.0.0:1883

# The diagnostics surface: /status, /mode, /queue, /secs, /labels, /inventory,
# /reconciliation, /promotions, /rules, /pos/price.
#
# The binary's default is 127.0.0.1:8080. Bind it to the LAN only if a support
# engineer needs to reach it without an SSH tunnel, and understand what that
# means: /pos/price accepts price changes, and /mode changes whether the store
# is pricing autonomously.
USSLP_GATEWAY_ADDR=127.0.0.1:8090

# The obs admin surface: /metrics, /healthz, /readyz. Bound to the LAN so the
# region's Prometheus can federate it; /debug/pprof is absent because
# USSLP_ENABLE_PPROF is false below.
USSLP_ADMIN_ADDR=0.0.0.0:9090
USSLP_ENABLE_PPROF=false
USSLP_TRACE_SAMPLE_ONE_IN=100

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The cloud link
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Leave USSLP_CLOUD_BROKER_URL empty and the gateway logs "no cloud broker
# configured: this store will run permanently autonomous" and serves the store
# from its local rules forever. That is a valid single-store deployment and a
# catastrophic misconfiguration for a chain; there is no way to tell them apart
# from here, so the warning is the only signal.
USSLP_CLOUD_BROKER_URL=tls://mqtt.us-east-1.usslp.REPLACE-ME.example:8883

# Credentials, as files. The device credential is issued scoped to
# usslp/{your-tenant}/# — a single ACL rule that is complete isolation.
USSLP_MQTT_USERNAME_FILE=/etc/usslp/secrets/mqtt-username
USSLP_MQTT_PASSWORD_FILE=/etc/usslp/secrets/mqtt-password

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WAN failure detection
#
# These six values decide when a store stops trusting the cloud and starts
# pricing itself. Getting them wrong in either direction is expensive:
#
#   too sensitive — the store flips to autonomous on every broadband hiccup,
#                   and every flip produces reconciliation conflicts when the
#                   link returns;
#   too slow      — the store keeps waiting for a cloud that is not coming, and
#                   the labels show yesterday's prices while it waits.
#
# The defaults below (fail after 3 failures sustained over 12s, recover after 4
# successes sustained over 15s) are asymmetric on purpose: it should be easier
# to decide the cloud is gone than to decide it is back, because a flapping link
# that is treated as up produces a bridge that starts and stops repeatedly.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
USSLP_PROBE_INTERVAL=5s
USSLP_PROBE_TIMEOUT=3s
USSLP_WAN_FAIL_THRESHOLD=3
USSLP_WAN_FAIL_FOR=12s
USSLP_WAN_RECOVER_THRESHOLD=4
USSLP_WAN_RECOVER_FOR=15s

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The upstream buffer
#
# What the gateway holds while the WAN is down. When it fills, the cloud's
# record of the outage has gaps that no replay can recover — which is why the
# gateway's own readiness check says exactly that, and why the alert on it is a
# page rather than a warning.
#
# 50,000 entries at 256 MB is roughly a day of a normal store's upstream
# traffic. A hypermarket, or a store with a known-bad line, should raise both.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
USSLP_QUEUE_MAX_ENTRIES=50000
USSLP_QUEUE_MAX_MB=256

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# State and keys
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
USSLP_DATA_DIR=/var/lib/usslp

# The key ring the gateway holds for verifying attestations locally. Optional:
# without it the gateway bridges attested updates through without checking
# them, and the controller — which recomputes the digest itself and is the
# authority — still refuses anything that does not verify.
USSLP_KEYRING_FILE=/etc/usslp/secrets/keyring.json

# The local price authority, for autonomous mode. When the cloud is unreachable
# the store prices from its own rules, and those prices still have to be signed
# or the controllers will refuse them. Leave empty and the store cannot change
# a price while it is autonomous — which is a defensible choice, and a
# deliberate one, not a default to drift into.
USSLP_LOCAL_AUTHORITY_DIR=/etc/usslp/secrets/local-authority

# Drain. Must be shorter than the unit's TimeoutStopSec (45s).
USSLP_SHUTDOWN_GRACE=20s
